Reference patch — ORT core ValidateExternalDataPath AppContainer guard
=======================================================================

Target: microsoft/onnxruntime @ tag v1.24.4 (matches Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime.DirectML
        1.24.4 pinned in uwp/packages.config).
File:   onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc  (ValidateExternalDataPath)

Problem (docs/uwp-constraints.md §8): loading an ONNX model with a separate
`.onnx.data` file triggers ValidateExternalDataPath, which calls
std::filesystem::weakly_canonical() on absolute paths. On the Xbox UWP
AppContainer, MSVC STL walks the path from the drive root and hits the
inaccessible Q:\Users\UserMgr0 segment → ACCESS_DENIED → exception → crash in
OgaCreateModel. The current workaround merges the weights into model.onnx, but
that fails above the 2 GB protobuf single-file ceiling, blocking fp16 models >2 GB.

Fix: replace the throwing one-arg weakly_canonical() calls with a guarded helper
that uses the std::error_code overload and falls back to lexically_normal() when
the filesystem walk is denied. The external-data file is a trusted, already-present
local file (GetFileAttributesW/CreateFile2 succeed per §8 diagnosis), so a lexical
normalization preserves the "external data must not escape the model dir"
containment check for the no-symlink/no-`..` case while avoiding the crashing walk.

Applied by scripts/vendor-ort-extdata-patch.ps1 (which prefers `git apply` and
falls back to a context-tolerant in-place transform, then verifies the change is
present before building). If `git apply` rejects this reference diff because
upstream context drifted, regenerate it against the pinned checkout — the semantic
change is the four edits below.

--- a/onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/framework/tensorprotoutils.cc
@@ namespace onnxruntime {
+// xllama (AppContainer): std::filesystem::weakly_canonical() walks path segments
+// from the drive root and throws ACCESS_DENIED on the inaccessible
+// Q:\Users\UserMgr0 segment (docs/uwp-constraints.md §8), crashing model load.
+// Use the std::error_code overload and fall back to a purely lexical
+// normalization when the walk is denied — the external-data file is a trusted
+// local file that already exists.
+static std::filesystem::path XllamaSafeCanonical(const std::filesystem::path& p) {
+  std::error_code ec;
+  std::filesystem::path r = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(p, ec);
+  if (ec || r.empty()) {
+    return p.lexically_normal();
+  }
+  return r;
+}
+
 Status ValidateExternalDataPath(const std::filesystem::path& base_dir,
                                 const std::filesystem::path& location,
                                 const std::filesystem::path& model_path) {
@@ ValidateExternalDataPath
-    auto base_canonical = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(base_dir);
+    auto base_canonical = XllamaSafeCanonical(base_dir);
@@
-    auto resolved = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(base_dir / location);
+    auto resolved = XllamaSafeCanonical(base_dir / location);
@@
-        auto real_model_dir = std::filesystem::weakly_canonical(model_path).parent_path();
+        auto real_model_dir = XllamaSafeCanonical(model_path).parent_path();
